# The 196 curse: flip a number's digits and add (196 + 691 = 887), then repeat.
# Most numbers soon read the same both ways, like 121. Nobody knows if 196 ever does.
# This hunt flags every number that is still not a palindrome after "limit" flips.
# A copycat lands on the path of an earlier cursed number (295 + 592 = 887, just like 196),
# so it is cursed for the same reason. A new family is one that joins nobody.
: limit 100 ;
: top 1000 ;
: rev 0 swap [ dup 10 % rot 10 * + swap 10 / ] drop ;
# cells: 2 where the number has got to, 7 that flipped, 3 flips so far, 8 whose path it landed on,
# 4 and 5 the toughest escape, 6 cursed so far, 1 families (their first numbers in -101, -102...). Every number on a family's path is
# marked in cell (number + 10) with 1000 x the family's first number + its place on that path.
# Landing on a path stops the walk early only when the rest of the walk is a stretch of that path
# already checked; otherwise it keeps flipping, so copycats never change who is cursed.
# The marks use seabed cells far past 2^62, so run this with `trawl run` (or the playground), not `trawl fast`.
: cell 10 + ;
: look 2 dig rev 7 bury  2 dig cell dig 13 bury
  13 dig if
    8 dig 0 = if 13 dig 1000 / 8 bury then
    13 dig 1000 % dup 0 >  swap 3 dig > 0 =  * if 1 14 bury then
  then ;
: going 2 dig 7 dig = 0 =  3 dig limit <  *  14 dig 0 =  * ;
: steps 0 3 bury 0 14 bury dup cell dig 1000 / 8 bury
  dup rev + 2 bury 1 3 bury look
  going [ drop 2 dig 7 dig + 2 bury 3 dig 1 + 3 bury look going ] drop
  14 dig if 0 else 2 dig 7 dig = if 3 dig else 0 then then ;
: mark dup 9 bury 2 bury 0 3 bury
  1 [ drop
    2 dig cell dig 0 = if 9 dig 1000 * 3 dig + 2 dig cell bury then
    2 dig dup rev + 2 bury  3 dig 1 + 3 bury  3 dig limit > 0 = ] drop ;
0 4 bury 0 5 bury 0 6 bury 0 1 bury
# the number being tested stays at the bottom of the stack, so "now at" shows it
1 1 [ drop
  dup steps dup 0 = if
    drop 8 dig if
      dup . ." is cursed, a copycat of " 8 dig . 10 emit
    else
      dup . ." is cursed: a new family, no palindrome after " limit . ." flips" 10 emit
      dup mark  1 dig 1 + 1 bury  dup -100 1 dig - bury
    then
    6 dig 1 + 6 bury
  else
    dup 4 dig > if 4 bury dup 5 bury else drop then
  then
  1 + dup top > 0 = ] drop drop
5 dig . ." broke free after " 4 dig . ." flips: the toughest escape" 10 emit
1 dig if
  1 dig dup . 1 = if ." cursed family, started by:" else ." cursed families, started by:" then
  32 emit 1 1 [ drop dup -100 swap - dig . 1 + dup 1 dig > 0 = ] drop drop 10 emit
  ." Tested every number up to " top . ." and found " 6 dig . ." cursed numbers: those families and their copycats" 10 emit
else
  ." Tested every number up to " top . ." and every one broke free" 10 emit
then
